WEBVTT

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:04.210
Ah, Muranushi...

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:05.540
How are you doing?

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.170
I see. Then I'd better not schedule
shifts for you yet, huh?

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.720
No, not at all. For now,
think of your health as number one.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.010
We'll make do somehow
with the staffers we have on hand.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.100
Um... The only thing is...

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.360
The super...

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.900
The supernatural events...

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.320
I mean, super-attendance award...

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.110
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.280
<i>There is no attendance award at work!
What am I talking about?</i>

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.960
Calm down.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.390
This is just awful.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.600
WE'RE ALL ILLING

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.100
Yeah, it's like this whenever Muranushi
is on an extended absence.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.440
Recently, we're being tormented
by some unseen thing.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:33.360
Maybe it's angry because we can't
communicate with it.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:34.820
I don't know...

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.070
but the person who caused
her absence has been safe

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:40.530
because of Muranushi's mother's
talisman. Isn't that probably it?

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.540
I-I said you can have the talisman...

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.580
No, you keep it.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.290
Lose that and you'll be murdered
by Muranushi's customer.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.090
Well, you know, right?

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:59.010
Where you should go
and what you should do, Adachi...

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.930
Yeah. Go to Muranushi's house and ask—

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:05.020
If you say "Ask for more talismans,"

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:08.270
I'll put this cigarette
through your eyeball.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.980
I was gonna say
"Ask after her health"!

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:12.650
Adachi!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.570
I have to leave early today.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.940
I heard!

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:18.740
You're going to visit Muranushi, right?

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.700
Oh, yeah.
That's where I'm heading now.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.370
Jeez. You're so inconsiderate.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:26.910
You were gonna go there empty-handed?

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.120
Sweets?

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.750
<i>Isn't it customary to bring fruit
for a get-well visit?</i>

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:33.380
Come back in one piece!

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:41.050
<i>Coming here was easy,
but will she agree to see me?</i>

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.100
<i>Adachi, you really are...</i>

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:48.890
<i>...a fool.</i>

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.400
Yes?

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.440
Excuse me.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:00.740
I'm Adachi, a co-worker
of Sayuri Muranushi.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.240
My sister is so sick...

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.120
that she doesn't really leave her room.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.000
<i>Her little brother?</i>

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.710
<i>He's got a hand on his shoulder!</i>

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.710
You're that Adachi. You came
just like Mom said you would.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.260
Please, come in.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:23.550
Thank you.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.510
Mom, Adachi is here!

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.060
Even though he caused
Sayuri's health to fail,

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.940
he came without shame.

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.310
Just like you said he would, Mom.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.070
<i>I'm having second thoughts about this!</i>

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.740
<i>Hang in there, me!</i>

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:43.700
Long time no see, Adachi.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.370
I'm surprised you've come.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.450
I know I have no business coming here,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.710
but I'm hoping
that you'll let me see your daughter.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:58.800
Oh, I just meant that I'm surprised
you knew our address.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:02.420
But either way, I'm afraid
I can't let you see Sayuri.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.050
I'm sorry.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:06.010
Sis needs her rest.

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.680
P-Please, can't you do something?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.600
After all, she has a 40-degree fever.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:13.140
40 degrees?

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:15.190
40 degrees is really high!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.440
Nothing you need to worry about.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.690
It seems she's just not herself lately.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.400
She'll be fine after an exorcism.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:22.690
SICK

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.400
<i>So she's not sick but possessed?</i>

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.400
POSSESSED

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.160
Sayuri, open up.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.120
You need to let me exorcise you.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.000
You'll die otherwise.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.080
Forget it.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:40.590
Come on. You'll never get better
until the cause of your illness is removed.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:46.510
In the first place,
the cause of this is you, Adachi.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:52.220
So if I defeat you, Sayuri will be cured.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.060
Stop it.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.270
Only Adachi can come in here.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:06.360
M-Muranushi...

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.740
Yes.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.450
Muranushi!

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.960
I did what I wanted to do.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:24.630
So I'm done with you. Go home.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:30.140
Muranushi! Do you have a cold?
Are you okay? Did you see a doctor?

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.430
Don't come near me.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:34.140
It's obvious, isn't it?

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:36.890
I'm not okay
and I haven't been to the doctor.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:38.140
You haven't?

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:41.860
When it's gotten this bad, you won't
get better unless you go to a doctor.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.860
I can't even muster the energy to go.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.150
C-Can't you have your family take you?

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:51.910
Scientific establishments
rub me the wrong way.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.910
Fine, Mother. Go away.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.330
After all, they stab you with needles.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:58.870
They're scary!

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.380
Anyway, we can't talk like this.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:04.090
Get dressed.

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:07.300
I'll take you to the doctor.

00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:08.800
Get out of here.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.760
I won't, Muranushi!

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.140
Get out of here.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:13.600
Muranushi!

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:18.560
I'm telling you to get out
so I can put some clothes on.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.690
You're flushed.
Have you caught her cold?

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:25.730
No.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.950
A-Are you okay?

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:37.620
If I were okay,
I wouldn't be going to the doctor.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.290
Sayuri, are you sure you won't let me
perform an exorcism on you?

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.290
After all, you're acting strange.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:45.960
You come staggering home from work,

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.630
then take a shower
which is a careless mist.

00:07:48.630 --> 00:07:51.630
it can only mean
you're possessed by something.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.930
Unless maybe you were shocked
at work about something?

00:07:58.430 --> 00:07:59.480
Muranushi!

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.400
I'm sorry! Would you please
go somewhere else?

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.400
Even though this is my house...

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:08.860
M-Muranushi...

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:14.240
Um, uh, about last time...

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:16.790
Th-That was, uh...

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:19.000
Express yourself in no uncertain terms.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.540
I told you to go away!

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:22.540
Muranushi...

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.500
Um...

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:29.340
<i>Man, if I don't take her to the doctor soon,
she'll get even worse</i>

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.090
<i>and we won't be able to talk,
so I need her to come out.</i>

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:36.470
<i>But if we don't talk about what happened
last time, nothing will be solved.</i>

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:39.770
<i>But what can I say to express
the way I feel clearly and concisely,</i>

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:42.190
<i>and get her to come out?</i>

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:49.650
Would you...

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.410
g-go out with me?

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.750
<i>She came out!</i>

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.470
Yeah, um, so...

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.090
our relationship is unclear
in various ways,

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.970
so I was thinking maybe we should
go out with each other to straighten it out.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:21.180
Why...

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.640
did you wait until now to bring that up?

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:24.640
40-DEGREE FEVER

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.150
Good point!

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.240
I'll go out with you.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:37.620
Adachi...

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.080
I can't hold back anymore.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.460
Right now, take me...

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:50.170
...to the doctor.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:51.960
Right, of course!

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.550
And so...

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.090
w-we're going out.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.350
I got better after going to the doctor.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:03.850
He made a sick person...

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.440
...agree to go out with him.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.310
Hey!

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.310
WHISPER WHISPER
WHISPER WHISPER

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:09.310
Muranushi!

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.190
I see.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.690
So those two are finally
going out, too, huh?

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.780
GRUMBLE RUMBLE

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.490
I mean, I'm hungry.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:20.410
But I don't have any money.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.290
I wanna put something in my tummy.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:30.000
Hime... I appreciate it, but I can't
take food from a growing child.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:32.960
By the way, Kisaki...

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.130
- Huh?
- Are you lactating?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:48.770
STOMP STOMP

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:38.050
I-I didn't mean...

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:41.180
I was just thinking that if you smoked,
breastfeeding would be bad for the baby!

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.430
But I wasn't implying
that you should feed me with it! Ow!

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.600
Either way, that was sexual
harassment, wasn't it? I'm sorry!

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.640
I'm just so hungry
that I can't control my thoughts!

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.980
So give me something to eat! Ow!

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.860
Shindou, there's no point
in begging Kisaki for food.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:56.070
I'll give you the leftover sweets
from my seminar.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.740
Want my rolled sushi?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.240
It's from my bento.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.120
God and Goddess!

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.290
Come to think of it, your family runs
a sushi shop, doesn't it?

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.410
That's right, but so what?

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:12.090
If you two get married in the future
and you take over the sushi shop,

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:14.920
can I come over to eat the leftovers?

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:15.670
Huh?

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:20.590
Adachi...

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:25.310
That long "Huh?" just now meant
you don't want to take over the sushi shop?

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:28.230
Or you don't want Shindou coming over
to scavenge for leftovers?

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:30.230
Or you don't want me to be your wife?

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:31.100
Which is it?

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.270
No, you've got the wrong idea...

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:34.020
Tell me, tell me, tell me...

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.020
I'm sorry!

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.940
Yay, rice! Yay, sweets!

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:40.160
Hey there!

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:44.950
Saitou, the gloomy former NEET
and my family's current bodyguard

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:49.410
who's been moping around for years
after Muranushi smiled at you...

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:51.620
That's too damn long!
What do you want?

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:55.880
I hear Muranushi and Adachi
are dating! Lost love for you!

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:57.210
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:11:59.090
Kondou told me.

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.720
You say lost love,
but that was a long time ago.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:06.850
In fact, right now, I feel disconnected
from reality like I married Satan.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.060
Don't cry!

00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:13.400
I was looking forward to tormenting you
while you were grieving over a lost love.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.020
Stop crying!

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:25.870
<i>I'm a little late.</i>

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.040
<i>I think Yanagiba is at the restaurant, but...</i>

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.500
HIGASHIDA

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:32.500
Higashida?

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.080
Nagata...

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.250
<i>Higashida, what's wrong?</i>

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:39.380
Yanagiba is down with a cold.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:42.880
Wh-What should I do?
Pay her a get-well visit?

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.350
Higashida, do you know
where Yanagiba lives?

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:48.600
<i>Where she lives?
You don't need to go there.</i>

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:51.520
What? That's not a nice thing to say!

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.310
It's cold of you, Higashida.

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.270
She's resting here at the restaurant.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.940
Ahem! Ahem!

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:59.570
That's no good, Yanagiba!

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.360
Ahem! Ahem!

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:06.830
I kind of overdid it that last time
at the Okinawa commodity exhibition.

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:08.620
That may have been the cause.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.160
Ahem! Ahem!

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:11.710
Yanagiba...

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.330
Sorry, Higashida. I insulted you.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:19.050
It's fine. I'm just happy
you came over, Nagata.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.380
H-Higashida... You mean...

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.720
You want me to look after her?

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:30.810
If I did it, I think
I would eventually punch her.

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:33.810
But you didn't kick Yanagiba out,

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:36.310
which tells me
you're worried about her, too!

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.690
Miss! Feel free to relax here
until you're better, okay?

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:43.150
Higashida! Does this
situation call for porridge?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:46.280
Should I give this customer
some porridge I've made?

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.030
No.

00:13:49.030 --> 00:13:51.580
Higashida, why did you
think it over for a moment?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:55.500
Yanagiba...

00:13:56.250 --> 00:14:00.710
<i>Maybe it's just my imagination, but
it seems like it's more than just a cold.</i>

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:03.260
Naga, you can go home.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:04.760
But...

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.720
I should bring you some water, right?

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.350
Um, excuse me!

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:13.140
<i>A normal person? What should I do?</i>

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.560
<i>He seems to be an unnaturally
normal person for this place!</i>

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:18.400
U-Um, could I have some water?

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:21.070
As you can see,
she's laid up with a cold.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.110
If possible, a pitcher.

00:14:23.110 --> 00:14:26.650
A-And I'll order something later,
but for now...

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.490
Don't ever come back again!

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.990
<i>There, he's strange after all!</i>

00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:34.450
PHEW!

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:34.450
<i>What is it about this restaurant
that attracts them?</i>

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:41.920
Hey Saiki, I heard you talking earlier
to that high school girl who's here a lot.

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:43.550
Did you get through to her?

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:45.800
I think, somewhat.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:49.050
They were talking about a cold
or water or something like that.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:52.010
So I told them,
"Don't ever come back again!"

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:53.600
Wait a minute.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:56.940
You know that means
"Don't come here ever again," right?

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:57.850
What?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.150
But didn't you say that
to a customer the other day?

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.480
Well, he's a different story.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.740
It's rude, so just don't say it
to a customer again.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.490
But the customer you said it to
looked really happy for some reason.

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.200
That's because...

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:14.290
How am I supposed
to explain this in English?

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:18.920
Shaiki grew up abroad,
so he can't really speak Japanese.

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:21.790
Really? No wonder...

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:24.130
I hope he understood
what I said before.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:25.260
Thank you for your patience.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:27.970
Good. It looks like I got through.

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.470
Thank you for the water...

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:33.180
...and magazine?

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:36.390
You... murder time!

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:40.600
Ah, to kill time! Thank you!

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.070
<i>Nagata's been through a lot,</i>

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.360
<i>so Saiki's butchery of Japanese
doesn't rattle her.</i>

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:50.320
<i>I kind of feel guilty about that.</i>

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:53.030
- Higashida...
- Yes?

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:57.540
Your friend, Saiki, is interacting
with customers, but is that okay?

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:04.290
It seems she isn't bothered by his
linguistic missteps, so I guess it's all right.

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.170
Is that right?

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.670
Shaiki, read this magazine.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:12.050
I don't mean about Saiki
making Japanese mistakes.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:17.060
Yanagiba, you shouldn't ask
the workers to do things like this.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:19.730
It'll help him study Japanese,
so it's ok—

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.440
"Special feature, female friends.

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.860
Readers write in for advice.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:28.570
I have a female friend
who kind of likes a guy.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:34.120
I was hoping that I could
use her to get closer to him.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:37.700
But the boy got
a different girlfriend,

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.870
so while I'm still friends
with that girl,

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:46.920
to be honest,
I'm a little tired of her.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:49.760
What should I do?"

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.510
"For your own sake, break off
the friendship right away!"

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:56.390
Why did he read that part so fluently?

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.850
Th-That problem sounds
kind of familiar, doesn't it?

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:01.600
But that one's different, right?

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:03.350
Yeah.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:08.860
If Higashi hadn't called you before,
I bet you wouldn't have come, Naga.

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:11.990
<i>I-Is that why she's gloomy?</i>

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.700
You've got it wrong, Yanagiba!

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.660
I was late coming here
because of school!

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.530
You've got the wrong idea, Yanagiba!

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:18.700
Yanagiba!

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.450
She's better!

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.250
Oh, I better clean up!

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:26.000
Y-Yanagiba, come out!

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.590
Nagata...

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:31.460
Did something happen
with Yanagiba or Saiki or both?

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:32.840
Higashida...

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:34.470
actually...

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:35.840
<i>I can't say it.</i>

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:38.600
It's okay! This is between women!

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:40.180
<i>Between women?</i>

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.770
Those regulars are incredible!

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:45.020
They were talking normally to Saiki!

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.900
You still aren't able to talk
to Saiki, Miyakoshi?

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.740
Even if the language is different,
you could at least greet him.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:55.280
You're incorrigible.
This is why you're so...

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:56.990
I can't say it. Never mind.

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.370
<i>Damn you, Higashida!</i>

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.370
<i>I'll conquer him with Japanese!</i>

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.040
Saiki!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:18.140
<i>In the end, my girlfriend has even lost
the ability to speak Japanese. Jeez...</i>

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:25.730
Um, Yanagiba, certainly, I came
because Higashida asked me to,

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:28.940
but I think this is a nice place
to just chill out,

00:18:29.190 --> 00:18:32.440
and though you're not the least bit
interested in going to school,

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:35.700
I have a pretty good time coming here!

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.160
I'm not tired of you!

00:18:37.660 --> 00:18:39.200
I mean, recently,

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:43.540
it's like I've even forgotten
that I came here for Higashida.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.250
- Naga...
- Y-Yes?

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:49.330
Is that any way for a young girl
in love to behave?

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.750
Wh-What are you telling me to do?

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:55.260
F-For now, let's put that aside.

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:58.010
Look at me, Yanagiba!

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:01.680
We're friends, aren't we?

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:03.890
Yanagiba!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:08.310
Good.

00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.020
I was worried.

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.900
After Higashi
and Hana-hana started dating,

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:16.820
I thought maybe you didn't really
want to come here anymore, Naga.

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:21.240
Yanagiba, you were being
considerate of my feelings.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:23.790
But I had nothing
to worry about, huh?

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:27.660
That's right, Yanagiba!
That has nothing to do with anything!

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:31.840
Then it shows that you don't really
like Higashi all that much, Naga.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:36.550
<i>It's hard to dispute that right now
with an "Of course I do."</i>

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.260
I worry about Higashida recently.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:43.140
It looks like things are going
from bad to worse for him.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.720
And it seems like he's going
through a lot of problems,

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.890
so I want him to become happy.

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:51.020
Higashi has been irritable
because of stress.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.900
He even gets the urge to kill me,
all because of misdirected anger.

00:19:54.190 --> 00:19:56.070
That's not misdirected.

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.900
He's directly angry at you, Yanagiba.

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.820
Anyway, it's bad for his mind and body,

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:06.370
so Higashida should give up that deadly
chocolate and loveless relationship.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.410
You're kind to a fault, Naga.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.000
I think if he and Miyakoshi
had mutual love for each other,

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:14.130
it would be a decent relationship, but...

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:16.340
Mutual love...

00:20:17.260 --> 00:20:19.090
<i>Bonk!</i>

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:22.390
<i>Sorry, darling!
I messed up another meal!</i>

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.430
<i>You're a screw-up, Hana!</i>

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:28.480
<i>I'm dying as we speak!</i>

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.640
A decent relationship...

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.600
Either way, it's insane.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:34.230
Anyway, Higashi...

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:40.240
Yanagiba, before anything else,
you need to get rid of that cold.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:43.620
Right. Although I feel a lot better already.

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.280
Thank you, Naga.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:53.830
I don't know what's going on, but
I'm glad you two have patched things up!

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:54.920
Yeah...

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.920
Was my care package
of sweets the deciding factor?

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:03.890
My mother threw it into my room.

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:04.640
Huh?

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:11.640
Those are the sweets
Adachi left here yesterday.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:14.400
No sense in letting them
go to waste, right?

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:22.280
SHADY

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:22.990
They're from a shady character,
so I'm purifying them first.

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:24.860
All right, let's eat them.

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.530
I don't want any sweets
that had to be purified first.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.660
They won't kill you. Eat.

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:35.040
You say it like they're just a couple of days
past the expiration date.

00:23:06.090 --> 00:23:09.390
And so, I've recovered from my cold,

00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:13.140
and I'm off to visit Naga
who caught it from me.

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:15.560
Aside from going to school,
you're an active person, huh?

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:17.270
Tell her I said to get well soon.

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:19.150
Roger that.

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:36.040
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:29.410
And so, I'm Kouno,
in charge of saying silly things.

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:30.870
I'm Saiki,
in charge of saying silly things.

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:31.830
Saiki?

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:34.120
Next time, "Howl at the Moon."

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:36.040
HOWL AT THE MOON
